<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>
      {[assigns[:page_title], "OpenResults"] |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1) |> Enum.join(" - ")}
    </title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/app.css"} />
    <%!--
      No script tag, and no CSRF meta tag to feed one. These pages are read
      only and carry no session, so there is no token to hand a client and
      nothing for JavaScript to do. Hundreds of phones load this over a
      playing hall's wifi; a result should be readable the moment the HTML
      lands.
    --%>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="page">
      <a class="brand" href={~p"/"}>OpenResults</a>
      {@inner_content}
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
